    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mason Estates are excited to present this exceptionally fine four-bedroom semi-detached home to the market. Offering well proportioned, light filled accommodation, and extending to approximately 156 sq.m. (not including the attic space), the property is further complimented by a large private rear garden, a substantial garage with power and laundry facilities, and a converted attic offering an excellent and very usable additional space.\n \nNo. 19 Dargle Road is a bright, spacious family home which has been very well maintained by the current owners and offers generous accommodation throughout, with excellent potential to further enhance the property to suit modern family living. Unlike many of the neighbouring properties, the garage has been retained in its original use, providing excellent secure storage and parking, while offering potential to extend, while the attic has been converted to create a fabulous additional room.\n \nThe accommodation briefly comprises of: a screened entrance porch leading into a spacious entrance hall, with stairs rising to the first floor, useful under-stairs storage and access to the downstairs WC. To the front of the property is the bright and generously proportioned living room, with a large front window ensuring plenty of natural light. Double doors lead through to the separate dining room, creating an excellent space for both everyday family life and entertaining.\n \nTo the rear is the well-proportioned modern kitchen, with good storage and worktop space, and access to the rear garden. The kitchen also benefits from excellent natural light and is positioned overlooking the garden, while there is a patio, and deck area immediately outside, providing a natural extension of the living accommodation during the warmer months.\n \nThe large private rear garden, circa 22m x 10.5m is a wonderful feature of the property. There is a generous patio area, ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining, with the remainder of the garden providing excellent space for children, gardening and family use. The garden also offers potential to extend the existing accommodation, subject to the necessary planning permission. There is a patio sun-trap at the rear of the garden ideal for summer dining, and catching the last of the evening light, and a useful garden shed.\n \nThe garage is accessed from the front with a roller shutter, and the rear garage door, and measures approximately 5.46m x 2.58m. It remains in use as a garage and benefits from power and laundry facilities, making it an extremely practical addition to the property and provides excellent storage. There is excellent potential to extend the house into the garage, with precedent along the road.\n \nUpstairs there are four well-proportioned bedrooms and the family bathroom. The master bedroom is a particularly generous room and benefits from excellent storage, and en-suite shower room. The second bedroom is another good-sized double room, while the third and fourth bedrooms are both well-proportioned and offer excellent flexibility for family accommodation, guest bedrooms or home office use.\n \nThe modern family bathroom is located off the landing and serves the remaining bedrooms. The bright and spacious landing provides access to all four bedrooms and also leads to the stairs to the converted attic.\n \nThe attic has been converted to create a large, bright and extremely usable additional room measuring approximately 3.87m x 6.02m, which could be used in a variety of ways, including as a home office, playroom, games room, hobby room or simply as superb additional storage. There is also under eaves storage on both sides of the room.\n\nThe property has GFCH, a strong C BER rating, is alarmed, is wired for high speed internet, and has off-street parking for 2 cars.\n \nDargle Road is a popular residential development located just off Newtown Park Avenue, close to the N11 and within walking distance of Stillorgan and Blackrock villages and all their excellent amenities, while the Dunnes Stores and 24-hour Centra on Newtownpark Avenue are just around the corner.\n \nThe property is in the catchment area for several outstanding primary and secondary schools, including Holly Park, Carysfort NS and the Guardian Angels, and secondary schools including Newpark Comp, Oatlands, Blackrock College, CBC Monkstown, Loreto Foxrock, St Andrews College and Sion Hill, to name a few.\n \nThere are also numerous local sports clubs close by with the Granada Football Club in Holly Park, Blackrock Rugby Club in Stradbrook, and Kilmacud Crokes in Stillorgan Village. Newtown Park, Carysfort Park and Rockfield Park, with their numerous tennis and sports clubs, are all a short stroll away.\n \nThe area is also well serviced by public transport, with the 114 bus running from Blackrock DART Station up to Sandyford, while the N11 is approximately a ten-minute walk with a bus every 10 minutes into the city centre. The L25 bus stop to Dundrum is around the corner on St Augustine`s, and the M50 is a five-minute drive away.\n \nIn short, No. 19 Dargle Road is a fabulous family home, in a quiet and highly convenient residential location, which offers both excellent family accommodation with excellent potential for the future, and viewing is highly recommended. To arrange a viewing please contact Ryan O`Shaughnessy or call the office on 01 2951001.\n \nACCOMMODATION\nTotal Floor Area: 156 sq. m. approximately\nExcluding screened porch, attic, and other areas as indicated on the floor plan.\n \nSCREENED PORCH: 1.13m x 1.71m\nEnclosed screened entrance porch leading to the entrance hall.\n \nENTRANCE HALL: 4.69m x 2.47m\nSpacious entrance hall providing access to the house, with stairs rising to the first floor.\n \nGUEST WC: 1.74m x 0.84m\nConvenient guest w.c. with floor to ceiling tiles.\n \nLIVING ROOM: 4.00m x 5.30m\nBright and spacious reception room with generous proportions, a wood burning stove, and large window overlooking the front garden. Double doors lead through to the dining room. \n \nDINING ROOM: 3.90m x 4.24m\nWell-proportioned dining room, adjoining the kitchen, with a wood burning stove, access to the rear garden and deck area.\n \nKITCHEN: 4.44m x 3.23m\nGood-sized kitchen with fitted floor and wall units, Bosch double oven and built-in microwave, gas hob, ample worktop space, and access to the rear garden.\n \nGARAGE: 5.46m x 2.58m\nExcellent-sized garage retained in its original use, with power and laundry facilities. Provides excellent secure storage and with access to the side of the property. \n \nMASTER BEDROOM: 3.46m x 4.24m\nFine spacious double bedroom overlooking the front of the property, with excellent built-in storage and an en-suite shower room.\n \nEN-SUITE: 1.61m x 1.47m\nEn-suite shower room with floor to ceiling tiles, shower unit, w.c. and w.h.b.\n \nBEDROOM 2: 3.47m x 3.14m\nGenerous double bedroom with built-in wardrobes.\n \nBEDROOM 3: 3.50m x 2.40m\nWell-proportioned bedroom overlooking the front of the property.\n \nBEDROOM 4: 2.37m x 3.24m\nFurther well-proportioned bedroom with built-in wardrobes and excellent potential for use as a bedroom, or home office.\n \nFAMILY BATHROOM: 2.41m x 1.84m\nGood-sized family bathroom with floor to ceiling tiles a bath with a glass shower door, w.c. and w.h.b. with under sink storage.\n \nLANDING: 3.01m x 4.34m\nSpacious first-floor landing providing access to all four bedrooms, family bathroom and stairs to the attic.\n \nATTIC ROOM: 3.87m x 6.02m\nExcellent converted attic space providing excellent potential for use as a home office, playroom, hobby room, games room or additional storage.\n \nPATIO: 7.12m x 6.75m\nGenerous patio area providing an excellent space for outdoor dining and entertaining.\n \nDECK: 3.38m x 3.56m\nRaised deck area providing an additional outdoor seating or entertaining space.\n \nSHED: 0.77m x 0.94m\nUseful garden storage shed."
      },
